diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1ae8deb..0fed02e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -34,6 +34,19 @@ When something goes wrong, it **recovers** instead of failing silently:
 - **Ghost rider:** unacknowledged reservations time out, uncollected stock is released and reassigned. Collected cargo is never "released" back to stock.
 - **Mid-route shelter change:** cargo already on the road is rerouted to the safest alternative shelter. If none exists, it is marked **At Risk** with an urgent alert — an unsafe delivery is never forced.
 
+## Sign-in and roles
+
+Everyone signs in before using the app. Each role sees only what it needs:
+
+| Role | Can do | Demo login |
+|---|---|---|
+| Operations admin | Everything: dispatch, riders, shelters, simulator, logs | `admin@rescueflow.org` / `admin123` |
+| Donor | List and manage their own donations | `donor@sunrise.org` / `donor123` |
+| Volunteer rider | See their own jobs; accept, pick up, deliver | `rider@rescueflow.org` / `rider123` |
+| Shelter coordinator | Update their shelter's demand, resources and status | `shelter@riverside.org` / `shelter123` |
+
+New donors, riders and shelter coordinators can create their own accounts from the sign-in page. Accounts are stored in the browser with hashed passwords — a prototype only; a real deployment would use a server-side login.
+
 ## Features
 
 - Operations dashboard: KPIs, live deliveries, donation table, rider availability, shelter demand, urgent alerts, recent events
